onument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Nart sagas are a body of epic tales from the North Caucasus, told among the Ossetians, Circassians, Abkhaz, Abazins, Karachays, Balkars, Chechens and Ingush.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/nartiang"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/nartiang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Nartiang</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Nartiang is a village in the West Jaintia Hills of Meghalaya, north-east India, once a summer seat of the Jaintia kings.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/narva"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/narva.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Narva</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Narva is a city in north-eastern Estonia on the Narva river, which forms the border with Russia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/narwar"><span class="enc-name">Narwar</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Narwar is a town in the Shivpuri district of Madhya Pradesh, India, on the Sindh river, below a large hilltop fort.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/naryn-kala"><span class="enc-name">Naryn-Kala</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Naryn-Kala is the citadel of Derbent, in Dagestan, Russia, on a hill above the city and the Caspian Sea.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/naser-al-din-shah-qajar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/naser-al-din-shah-qajar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Naser al-Din Shah Qajar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Naser al-Din Shah was the Qajar shah of Iran from 1848 to 1896, the longest reign of the dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclop